WEBVTT

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.360
<b>Colonel</b>

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:14.610
This program is a work of fiction. 
The characters, organizations, locations, laws, names, 
etc. being portrayed are unrelated to actual events.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:11.360
Remember that, as the 
protection of the state and

00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:15.200
the maintenance of its power depend 
upon the strength of its arms,

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.600
the growth or decline of this strength

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.840
must affect the nation's destiny, 
for good or for evil.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.460
Therefore neither be led astray by 
current opinions nor meddle in politics,

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:25.620
<b>Young Heroes</b>

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:28.460
but with single heart fulfill 
your essential duty of loyalty,

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.850
and bear in mind that duty is 
weightier than a mountain,

00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:34.220
while death is lighter than a feather.

00:00:34.490 --> 00:00:36.840
Remember that, as the 
protection of the state and

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:40.350
the maintenance of its power depend 
upon the strength of its arms,

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:42.620
the growth or decline of this strength

00:00:42.620 --> 00:00:45.250
must affect the nation's destiny, 
for good or for evil.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:48.190
Therefore neither be led astray by 
current opinions nor meddle in politics,

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:52.400
but with single heart fulfill 
your essential duty of loyalty,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.220
and bear in mind that duty is 
weightier than a mountain,

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:58.810
while death is lighter than a feather.

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:04.430
<i>As the embers of world war smoldered</i>

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.600
<i>in autumn of 1937,</i>

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.950
<i>the Imperial Army</i>

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:12.210
<i>established a clandestine spy training agency.</i>

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.210
<b>Greater East Asia
Cultural Society</b>

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:15.300
<i>The histories, names, and even ages</i>

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:19.490
<i>of the elite men who pass its 
rigorous application process</i>

00:01:19.490 --> 00:01:22.510
<i>are all treated as top-secret information.</i>

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.290
<i>They easily complete training 
exercises that push them</i>

00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:28.650
<i>to their physical and mental limits.</i>

00:01:28.970 --> 00:01:31.480
<i>Under the command of founder 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.860
<i>they operate worldwide, 
within the shadows.</i>

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.380
<i>And so a brand-new intelligence 
agency was created.</i>

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.300
<i>Its name is "D-Agency."</i>

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.420
Episode 2: Joker Game (Part 2)

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:17.760
Are you even Japanese?!

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:18.800
Lieutenant!

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.180
Order them to take off their shoes!

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.300
Stop! Stop it!

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.640
What're you looking for?!

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.810
Are you trying to break my house?

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.930
Oh, no, knock it off! Hey, that's my treasure!

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.520
Don't even touch it!

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.480
Hey, are you listening?!

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:37.340
I've had enough of you people.

00:03:37.690 --> 00:03:39.250
Once was bad enough,

00:03:39.570 --> 00:03:41.590
but twice is unforgivable!

00:03:42.790 --> 00:03:44.620
What'd you say? Twice?

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.200
What do you mean?!

00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.060
The kitchen is clear.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.560
The yard is clear.

00:03:50.860 --> 00:03:52.390
Drawers are clear.

00:03:52.690 --> 00:03:54.460
Above the ceiling is clear.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:04:00.400
<i>There wasn't anything here</i>

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:03.430
<i>for us to find in the first place!</i>

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:06.580
What's the matter, Captain-san?

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.890
Is it show time now?

00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:19.460
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:25.300
<i>I'm the one who ended up</i>

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:29.790
<i>drawing the joker?!</i>

00:04:59.650 --> 00:05:02.290
Kill or commit suicide...

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.530
The worst possible decisions a spy can make.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:10.230
Ah, so spies are cowards, huh?

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:13.080
We...

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:16.170
weren't playing poker at all.

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:20.330
Japan was preoccupied with 
the rules for the façade.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:24.790
We never even noticed the true 
nature of the game being played.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:29.740
Tautology. "With enough faith,
you can worship a sardine's head."

00:05:30.040 --> 00:05:32.010
It's a deeply entrenched belief...

00:05:33.240 --> 00:05:37.600
When these men leave here, 
they'll be scattered all over the world,

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:41.170
where they'll have to make themselves invisible.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:47.560
<i>Invisible people... Invisible places...</i>

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:50.660
<i>Invisible places?</i>

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:06.130
Come on, you can't quit now.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.930
Back of the imperial portrait.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:16.950
Sir!

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:20.500
<i>That's right.</i>

00:06:20.500 --> 00:06:25.260
<i>There's one place in Gordon's house 
that a real military policeman</i>

00:06:25.260 --> 00:06:27.780
<i>would never dare to touch.</i>

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:31.500
<i>It's in plain sight, yet 
invisible at the same time.</i>

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:35.060
<i>But an impostor MP,</i>

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:37.960
<i>someone from D-Agency...</i>

00:06:38.120 --> 00:06:40.250
Stop! Stop it!

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:42.670
<i>The man who organized them, 
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki,</i>

00:06:42.670 --> 00:06:44.380
<i>even if he never saw it in person...</i>

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:47.010
Hey, don't touch that!

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:51.690
<i>He understood that something was there.</i>

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:01.350
I have one question.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:04.380
Did you know that the real military police

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:08.370
had already searched Gordon's house?

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.700
What makes you think that?

00:07:12.490 --> 00:07:17.300
You always say that spies are invisible.

00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:19.750
The reason you dressed everyone up as MP

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:22.190
and sent them over in broad daylight was

00:07:22.190 --> 00:07:24.490
to make Gordon lower his guard,

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:28.170
so that the MP would have 
less trouble in the future.

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:34.940
Excuse me.

00:07:42.760 --> 00:07:43.940
Miyoshi...

00:07:45.850 --> 00:07:48.240
Heading back to the General Staff Office?

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:52.530
I'm sure the Colonel will be 
shocked to hear your report.

00:07:55.660 --> 00:07:57.280
Did you come here to mock me?

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:02.360
No. I've changed my opinion of you a bit.

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:05.740
I didn't think Sakuma-san the soldier

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:08.250
would have caught that.

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:10.210
More importantly,

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:15.210
we're going out on the town.

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:17.210
Would you care to join us?

00:08:17.650 --> 00:08:20.070
Maybe splurge and go to a classy restaurant?

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:22.090
Back there, why...

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:26.150
No, forget it.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:30.510
I'm afraid I'll have to pass. Maybe next time.

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.100
I see.

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:48.110
<i>I have no proof that Colonel Mutou 
commanded the military police</i>

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:50.980
<i>to search Gordon's house beforehand.</i>

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:54.360
<i>But if he didn't,</i>

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:58.820
<i>he must've been shaken by the fact 
that they didn't find anything.</i>

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:04.140
<i>If his failure were to go public,</i>

00:09:04.670 --> 00:09:08.390
<i>it would tarnish his record</i>

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:12.320
<i>and ruin his chances for further promotions.</i>

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.930
<i>It must have occurred to him then</i>

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.190
<i>that he could cover up his own failure by</i>

00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:26.740
<i>having someone else make the same mistake.</i>

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:31.550
<i>If someone else failed at the same task...</i>

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.430
<i>The question is,</i>

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:37.690
<i>how did Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki learn</i>

00:09:37.690 --> 00:09:40.530
<i>that Colonel Mutou had already 
raided Gordon's house?</i>

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:45.470
<i>The colonel would've kept that failure a secret.</i>

00:09:46.290 --> 00:09:49.320
<i>Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki only 
could've learned what happened</i>

00:09:49.910 --> 00:09:52.470
<i>on the night the raid took place.</i>

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:58.530
<i>Come to think of it,</i>

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:01.060
<i>the day I went to the General Staff Office</i>

00:10:01.060 --> 00:10:03.920
<i>and received the order 
to search Gordon's home,</i>

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.330
<i>Colonel Mutou was clearly hungover.</i>

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:18.470
Maybe splurge and go to a classy restaurant?

00:10:27.310 --> 00:10:30.560
You... found proof?

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:34.260
Impossible... There's no way...

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:36.510
I wasn't told that it was the second time.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:41.060
What? What did you just say?

00:10:41.770 --> 00:10:44.240
Sir, yesterday,

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:47.140
you ordered me to use D-Agency

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:51.270
to search the home of the 
American spy John Gordon.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.890
However, I was not informed that the

00:10:53.890 --> 00:10:57.090
military police had already searched 
Gordon's home once before.

00:10:57.710 --> 00:10:59.220
Of course not!

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:02.700
Listen. You're nothing more than

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.720
a liaison between us and those guys.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.430
You think I need to explain everything to you?

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:09.800
Keep your ego in check!

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.430
That doesn't matter.

00:11:13.230 --> 00:11:15.320
Tell me where you found the evidence.

00:11:15.320 --> 00:11:17.170
Yes, sir. If you'll excuse me...

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:22.310
Behind the imperial portrait.

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:25.170
Impossible!

00:11:25.170 --> 00:11:27.450
Don't tell me you went in and...

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:30.220
No, sir. I never laid a finger on it.

00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:37.790
Well, where's the microfilm you found?

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:40.040
We didn't bring back the evidence.

00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:40.970
What?!

00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:45.340
We only confirmed its existence. 
We didn't bring it back.

00:11:45.680 --> 00:11:48.560
You fool! What were you thinking?!

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.230
Then... I see.

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.810
The microfilm you found

00:11:54.810 --> 00:11:58.350
didn't contain any photos 
of army crypto ciphers.

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.780
No, that's exactly what it was.

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:06.400
What kind of imbecile

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:09.540
lets an enemy spy slip away 
with something like that?!

00:12:10.210 --> 00:12:13.760
Now that we've confirmed 
what codes were taken,

00:12:13.760 --> 00:12:15.880
if we change our encryption, it's harmless.

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:20.130
Rather, it benefits our own 
communications to let the enemy

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:22.720
waste their time with meaningless ciphers.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.880
That may be so.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:29.290
But what about that damned spy?

00:12:29.290 --> 00:12:32.730
You're not going to just let him 
swim back home, are you?

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:36.360
Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki is handling Gordon.

00:12:36.660 --> 00:12:38.980
He intends to use him as an asset.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:40.500
An asset?!

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:42.360
Yes, sir. He claimed he would

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:45.290
turn him into a double agent.

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:50.590
Damn it! Yuuki, you son of a bitch!

00:12:50.590 --> 00:12:52.740
This means he got the man,

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:55.370
the evidence, and all the glory!

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:57.280
An asset?! Shit!

00:12:57.280 --> 00:12:59.520
What does he think Gordon is?!

00:12:59.520 --> 00:13:01.710
People aren't toys, damn it!

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.360
I have something of yours, Colonel Mutou.

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:13.530
Something of mine?

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:21.620
Yeah, this is mine, all right.

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.460
Where'd you find it?

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:26.220
Apparently, it was on the floor 
in the hallway at Hanabishi.

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.910
H-Hanabishi?!

00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:39.380
Hanabishi

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.380
Welcome.

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:45.050
Hanabishi

00:13:40.030 --> 00:13:41.390
Welcome.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:47.050
Oh!

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:51.700
Is that... Sakuma-san?

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:55.310
I'm here on a secret investigation.

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:57.520
I have a few questions for you.

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:05.000
Yes, Mutou-san was here on that day.

00:14:05.000 --> 00:14:08.040
How did he look to you at that time?

00:14:08.380 --> 00:14:11.130
He seemed to be in a terrible mood.

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:15.660
He was here drinking until very late at night.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:20.020
Can you tell me about the other 
customers present, if there were any?

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:22.660
Oh, there was

00:14:23.010 --> 00:14:27.010
a man in the next room who 
drank too much and fell asleep.

00:14:27.850 --> 00:14:29.640
Can you describe him?

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:32.580
He's the president of a small trading company

00:14:32.880 --> 00:14:36.330
who comes to this establishment quite often.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:38.750
He's a very sociable man

00:14:39.050 --> 00:14:41.790
who's always making our 
younger geishas laugh.

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:48.770
Certainly not anyone suspicious.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.060
Does he have

00:14:52.670 --> 00:14:55.080
any distinctive traits?

00:14:55.890 --> 00:14:56.620
For example,

00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:00.080
does he walk with a cane due to a lame left leg?

00:15:00.080 --> 00:15:04.660
Or wear a white leather glove on his right hand?

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:11.480
I see...

00:15:14.860 --> 00:15:16.470
I'll be on my way, then.

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:18.820
Sorry to disturb you when you're busy.

00:15:19.150 --> 00:15:20.750
Oh, that's right!

00:15:20.750 --> 00:15:23.900
Now that you mention it, that night,

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:26.940
he turned in something 
Mutou-san had dropped.

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:29.740
A cigarette case.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.620
It was empty, so I held on to it.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.110
If you're returning to headquarters,

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:39.630
would you mind bringing it to him?

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.730
It's against military law to tell anyone

00:15:47.500 --> 00:15:51.800
the details of a military police raid 
on a suspected enemy spy's home,

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:54.130
even a geisha whom you visit regularly.

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.450
Furthermore, Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki

00:16:01.450 --> 00:16:04.980
has stated that this matter 
will not be made public.

00:16:05.360 --> 00:16:07.900
This concludes my report.

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:10.690
You bastard...

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:14.700
When did you switch to their side?

00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:19.670
I am simply acting as a liaison,

00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:22.870
as per the orders I was given.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:24.870
Get out.

00:16:24.870 --> 00:16:25.470
Huh?

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:27.960
I said, get out!

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:30.630
Yes, sir! Excuse me!

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:20.040
Miyoshi was impressed with you.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:23.430
You were

00:17:23.940 --> 00:17:27.020
really going to cut open your 
stomach there, weren't you?

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:31.230
<i>It's probably true that Miyoshi was impressed.</i>

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:32.530
<i>Still...</i>

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:36.440
<i>They noticed the second half of 
the situation well in advance.</i>

00:17:37.350 --> 00:17:40.610
<i>I never would've considered 
that Colonel Mutou</i>

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:44.540
<i>might have set all this up 
to cover his own mistake.</i>

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:49.000
<i>To the very end, I wasn't able to even join in</i>

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:51.450
<i>the Joker Game...</i>

00:17:53.810 --> 00:17:56.430
That cane is a disguise, isn't it?

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:02.010
You've been asking questions.

00:18:06.500 --> 00:18:07.380
For example,

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:10.600
does he walk with a cane due to a lame left leg?

00:18:10.600 --> 00:18:15.780
Or wear a white leather glove on his right hand?

00:18:19.290 --> 00:18:21.730
You can walk perfectly well without a cane.

00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:25.810
You wear a white leather glove 
when you walk with the cane.

00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:30.270
Having such a memorable, 
conspicuous appearance makes it

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.060
easier to disguise yourself.

00:18:32.930 --> 00:18:34.530
And as a result,

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:37.190
your less noticeable left hand

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:39.430
is much more readily overlooked.

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:43.970
Your left hand is a prosthetic, isn't it?

00:18:47.940 --> 00:18:51.400
I had a forensic expert at the imperial 
university do an examination for me.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.000
There were no fingerprints

00:18:54.000 --> 00:18:56.320
on the front of the cigarette case.

00:18:57.700 --> 00:19:00.490
Or to be more specific, Colonel Mutou's,

00:19:00.940 --> 00:19:02.440
the Hanabishi proprietress's,

00:19:03.660 --> 00:19:05.220
and my fingerprints

00:19:05.220 --> 00:19:07.870
were the only ones that were detected.

00:19:09.960 --> 00:19:10.850
In other words,

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:15.440
the only fingerprints missing were those 
of the customer who turned in the case.

00:19:17.470 --> 00:19:20.400
Wearing a glove on your right hand

00:19:20.400 --> 00:19:23.300
leads people to believe that's the injured hand.

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:26.950
But in reality, it was your left hand that you lost

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.770
during a past mission.

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.500
That jackass Mutou...

00:19:36.850 --> 00:19:40.830
Even I didn't expect him to be
idiotic enough to get drunk,

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:44.610
start blabbing about state 
secrets to a geisha,

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:47.380
then finish by dropping 
his property in the hall.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:51.190
Immediately after Mutou left,

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:54.500
I went out into the hall and 
saw his cigarette case.

00:19:55.730 --> 00:19:58.580
My right arm was wrapped around a geisha.

00:19:59.150 --> 00:20:00.420
In that scenario,

00:20:00.830 --> 00:20:03.840
it would've been unnatural not 
to pick it up with my left hand.

00:20:05.170 --> 00:20:08.210
I gave it to the proprietress 
and left for the night,

00:20:08.510 --> 00:20:11.180
but I didn't anticipate you having it examined.

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:16.890
Now that we've done him a favor,

00:20:16.890 --> 00:20:20.110
Mutou has no choice but to 
cooperate with D-Agency.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:24.510
We're a poor group with a very 
small budget, after all.

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:31.060
<i>Lieutenant Colonel Yuuki was 
shadowing Colonel Mutou</i>

00:20:31.530 --> 00:20:34.610
<i>to drag more funding out 
of the General Staff Office!</i>

00:20:43.210 --> 00:20:44.250
Do you

00:20:45.750 --> 00:20:48.220
have any interest in taking our training?

00:20:54.630 --> 00:20:57.690
I'm a soldier through and through.

00:20:58.350 --> 00:21:01.900
I'm prepared to sacrifice 
myself at a moment's notice.

00:21:03.610 --> 00:21:04.360
However...

00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:32.590
However,

00:21:36.850 --> 00:21:40.840
I refuse to be a pawn who 
is used, then cast aside.

00:23:19.960 --> 00:23:23.840
<b>Preview</b>

00:23:21.730 --> 00:23:23.750
You remember that incident now?

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:25.370
No...

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:27.130
Don't worry about it.

00:23:27.600 --> 00:23:29.550
The memories aren't important.

00:23:29.800 --> 00:23:34.880
Episode 3: Miscalculation

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:34.140
That was the right decision.
